Module admitted "A gate a rule opens" {
  Place court "the outer court" is settlement.
  Place lane "the lane" is room within court at 0, 0.
  Place porch "the porch" is room within court at 1, 0.
  Place hall "the hall" is room within court at 2, 0.
  Company party "You" of 1 at lane.
  Passage walk "the walk" is path between lane and porch.
  // The gate's opening is declared before the rule that admits the company (Low Water's 1, What Tessary Owes' W10).
  Passage inner "the inner gate" is gate between porch and hall
    opening when admitted(party) "The inner gate is barred.".
  Relation admitted(group).
  Rule admit when at(party, porch) and not admitted(party) says "The porter sees you on the porch and lifts the bar." { Assert admitted(party). }
  Observe porch_scene at porch when true "A stone porch before the inner gate.".
}
